     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This line doesn&#39;t do anything, just don&#39;t specify group.equal if there are no parameters to equate.</div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">equal </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;configural&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></code></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t think there is any reason to use simsem.  Look into<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ?cfaList</font>.  You can specify the data-generating function as the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">dataFunction= </font>argument and save the fit stats/indices using the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> FUN= </font>argument.</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423278234000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zX6Xsibnf4nvRab6i59I4\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
